<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>
  <!--
    Draws Odyssey's cerebrex node (Apparel_CerebrexNode) over a warcasket's shell on a pilot seen
    from behind, where the shell would otherwise cover it whole. Always on, whichever art the
    cerebrex art setting picks, and for every VFEP warcasket, ours or not.

    The node is a utility pack with no drawData of its own, so vanilla hands it one
    (DynamicPawnRenderNodeSetup_Apparel.ProcessApparel): layer 93 facing north, over a
    shell's 88, and -3 facing south, behind the body. A node's altitude is that layer times
    0.000366 (PawnRenderUtility.AltitudeForLayer, clamped to layer 100, so 0.0366 at most) plus
    its drawData offset y; "Draw order" in WarcasketShoulders_Overlord.xml's header has the
    arithmetic. VFEP's bases order the warcasket pieces by that offset, far past anything a layer
    can reach: facing north the armor sits at 0.1 (0.107 to 0.109 with its layer) and the
    shoulders at 0.2 (0.207 to 0.209), both over the pack's 0.034.

    A def's drawData replaces vanilla's default whole, so this one restates the two layers and
    adds the north offset. East and west stay unlisted, as in vanilla's: the pack keeps its place
    among the body apparel there, hanging out behind the back from under the shell.
    - North y 0.1, the armor base's own lift, which lands the pack at 0.134: 0.025 over any
      armor and 0.073 under any shoulders. Under the shoulders by choice. The node sits in the
      hollow of the Overlord's back between the pauldrons, whose inner edges cross its frame;
      drawn over them, the frame cuts across their outlines and the node reads as stuck on
      rather than seated.
    Without a warcasket nothing changes: on that facing the pack already drew over every graphic
    of the pawn, no vanilla or DLC node taking a north layer over its 93 (the status overlay's
    100 positions its own draws and ignores the node's altitude). Odyssey's outfit stand
    (Building_OutfitStand.RecacheGraphics) reads only the layer, then sets a pack's to the same
    93 and -3 itself.

    The root is gated on Odyssey's package id (LoadFolders.xml), so the xpath never misses;
    Tests/1.6/CerebrexNodeDrawOrderTests.cs holds the layers to vanilla's and the offset between
    VFEP's two.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "Apparel_CerebrexNode"]/apparel</xpath>
    <value>
      <drawData>
        <dataNorth>
          <layer>93</layer>
          <offset>(0, 0.1, 0)</offset>
        </dataNorth>
        <dataSouth>
          <layer>-3</layer>
        </dataSouth>
      </drawData>
    </value>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
